  "description": "External alterations including rendering, timber framing and replacement windows (part retrospective)",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;The replacement windows and\r\nassociated external alterations to the façade of the building by reason of\r\ninappropriate scale, proportions, detailing, and design, together with the\r\nremoval of original architectural features has resulted in an unsympathetic and\r\nvisually harmful alteration to the host building. &amp;nbsp;The development fails\r\nto preserve or enhance the character and appearance of the surrounding Moss\r\nLane Conservation Area and causes harm to the architectural integrity and\r\nproportions of the building. &amp;nbsp;As such, the development is contrary to the\r\nstatutory duty under Section 72 (1) of the Planning (Listed Buildings and\r\nConservation Areas) Act 1990, section 16 of the National Planning Policy\r\nFramework (2024), Policy HC1 of the London Plan (2021), Policies GR1 and HE1 of\r\nthe Harrow Local Plan 2021-2041 (2026), and guidance in the Moss Lane\r\nConservation Area Appraisal and Management Strategy (2009).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
